.TH GEOME 1 "2026-09-17" "geome" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
geome \- display approximate public IP-based location
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B geome
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B geome
uses the external HTTPS IP-geolocation service https://ipwho.is/ to locate
the public IP address used by its request. It does not determine GPS or
street-level location and does not discover the machine's physical position.
No IP address argument is sent. No root privileges are needed.
.PP
Requests have a 5-second connection timeout, a 10-second total timeout,
and a 1 MiB decompressed response limit. TLS peer and hostname verification
are enabled. Redirects, retries, caching, and provider fallback are disabled.
.SH OPTIONS
Select at most one output mode. Repeating the same mode is permitted.
Positional arguments and unknown options are errors.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-city
Print only the city. A missing city is an error; the region is not substituted.
.TP
.B \-\-coords
Print latitude,longitude with six fractional digits, no spaces or labels.
Both coordinates must be present. There is no short option.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print a single JSON object with all documented keys.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-full
Print labeled location fields, with Unknown for unavailable values.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help without network access. Help takes precedence over version.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version without network access.
.SH OUTPUT
The default is City, RegionCode, CountryCode. Missing codes fall back to full
names; unavailable components and their separators are omitted. At least one
city, region, or country identifier is required in every successful response.
.PP
JSON keys are city, region, region_code, country, country_code, lat, lon, ip,
and isp. Absent values are JSON null. Coordinates are numbers when present;
numeric zero is valid. Latitude is in [-90,90], longitude in [-180,180].
JSON key order is not an API guarantee. All successful outputs end with one
newline, use no ANSI colors, and have no accuracy prose added to the data.
.PP
Full output labels are City, Region, Region code, Country, Country code,
Latitude, Longitude, IP, and ISP, in that order. Diagnostics go to standard
error and start with geome:. A write failure can leave partial output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Network, DNS, connection, TLS, timeout, or truncated HTTP transfer failure.
.TP
.B 4
Remote service rejection, rate limit, or HTTP failure.
.TP
.B 5
Invalid, malformed, oversized, or incomplete location data.
.TP
.B 6
Local memory or internal failure.
.TP
.B 7
Output or diagnostic write failure, including a broken pipe.
.SH PRIVACY
Running the command sends a request from your public IP address to the provider.
The provider necessarily receives the public IP used for that request. The
request includes the geome name and version, an Accept header for JSON, and
supported content encodings. DNS and network intermediaries see connection
metadata; configured proxies can see additional information.
.PP
No user-created data, interface details, SSIDs, or MAC addresses are collected.
The program does not retain, log, or transmit the result elsewhere. It writes
the requested result to standard output and frees in-memory data on completion;
terminal history, redirection, swap, or system crash dumps are outside its control.
.SH ACCURACY
VPNs, proxies, corporate gateways, Tor, mobile routing, and ISP address
registration can produce a different city, region, or country. Never use IP
geolocation for emergency response, safety decisions, legal residency,
authentication, or precise tracking.
.SH FILES
None. Version 1 has no configuration or cache files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
There are no application-specific runtime configuration variables.
libcurl honors proxy variables including https_proxy, HTTPS_PROXY, all_proxy,
ALL_PROXY, no_proxy, and NO_PROXY. Proxy routing can change the apparent location.
Lowercase variants take precedence. Supported proxy schemes depend on libcurl.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
geome
geome --city
geome --coords
geome --json
geome --full
geome --help
geome --version
.fi
.SH BUGS
Provider availability, service limits, terms, and database accuracy can change.
Report reproducible defects to the repository owner using the contribution
instructions. Do not include your real public IP or unredacted location output.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR libcurl (3)
.PP
https://ipwhois.io/terms
